{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Remembered</b> — The sense: in every generation a remembrance is made of His wonders that He did in Egypt, for He is <b>gracious and compassionate</b> to show grace to those who cry out to Him, as in: \"and I will hear, for I am gracious\"."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 111, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:23.751381464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}